Authors of emeans

emeans is written and maintained by James Joseph Balamuta: the R port of
the algorithm, the C++ assignment kernels in src/, the torch backend, the
em_*() batch loop, the broom and tidyclust methods, the documentation and
the tests.

Ported code

The algorithm is ported from the Python implementation of e-means in faiss
contrib/e_means (https://github.com/facebookresearch/faiss), written by
Gergely Szilvasy, Swann Bessa and Matthijs Douze. The files derived from it
are listed in inst/COPYRIGHTS. They are credited as contributors for that
code only and took no part in writing, reviewing or maintaining this package,
so please report problems with it at
https://github.com/coatless-rpkg/emeans/issues.

Copyright holders

  James Joseph Balamuta, for the R package.

  Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates, for the faiss code from which the
  files listed in inst/COPYRIGHTS are derived, used under the MIT licence
  reproduced there.
